{
  "assessment": "The source provides a quantitative cluster for the incompressible kinetic energy E_i versus quench duration tau_Q at two temperatures (T=10^-6 and T=1), with fitted power laws and statistical details. The cluster is supported by the End Matter figure and text, and the reviewer figure evidence confirms the applicability interval [100,1000] for both branches. The extraction is complete and case_authoring_ready is true.",
  "case_authoring_ready": true,
  "source": {
    "citation": "Seong-Ho Shinn, Spontaneous Quantum Turbulence in a Newborn Bose-Einstein Condensate via the Kibble-Zurek Mechanism, Physical Review Letters (2026), DOI:10.1103/b16v-hwp2",
    "journal_doi": "10.1103/b16v-hwp2",
    "arxiv_versioned_id": "2506.21670v3"
  },
  "paper_scope": "The paper studies spontaneous quantum turbulence (SQT) in a 2D Bose-Einstein condensate formed by a thermal quench, using stochastic projected Gross-Pitaevskii simulations. It establishes Kibble-Zurek scaling of vortex number and equilibration time, Kolmogorov scaling of the incompressible kinetic energy spectrum, and universal collapse of spectra under KZ rescaling. The End Matter provides fits for the total incompressible kinetic energy E_i versus quench duration tau_Q at two temperatures.",
  "mechanisms": [
    {
      "mechanism_id": "kzm_ei_scaling",
      "statement": "The incompressible kinetic energy E_i at equilibration scales with quench duration as E_i proportional to tau_Q^{-(1+2 nu)/(1+z nu)}, derived from vortex number scaling n_v proportional to tau_Q^{-2 nu/(1+z nu)} and background density rho proportional to tau_Q^{-1/(1+z nu)}.",
      "equations": [
        "E_i \\propto \\tau_Q^{-(1+2\\nu)/(1+z\\nu)}",
        "E_i \\simeq (1/2) n_v \\int_{\\mathcal{D}_{\\hat{\\xi}}} |\\boldsymbol{u}_v|^2 d^2r"
      ],
      "variable_names": ["E_i", "tau_Q", "nu", "z", "n_v", "rho", "hat_xi", "u_v"],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "nu_critical_exponent",
          "value": 0.5,
          "uncertainty": "source_unspecified",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "correlation-length critical exponent",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 167,
              "line_end": 167,
              "support": "Using the mean-field values of the critical exponents nu = 1/2 and z = 2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "z_dynamic_exponent",
          "value": 2,
          "uncertainty": "source_unspecified",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "dynamic critical exponent",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 167,
              "line_end": 167,
              "support": "Using the mean-field values of the critical exponents nu = 1/2 and z = 2"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 314,
          "line_end": 328,
          "support": "At equilibration, background density rho proportional to tau_Q^{-1/(1+z nu)} and hat_xi proportional to tau_Q^{nu/(1+z nu)}, so each vortex contributes integral proportional to tau_Q^{-1/(1+z nu)}; combining with n_v proportional to tau_Q^{-2 nu/(1+z nu)} yields E_i proportional to tau_Q^{-(1+2 nu)/(1+z nu)}."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 414,
          "line_end": 417,
          "support": "Equation (eq:scaling_E_i_nu_z): E_i proportional to tau_Q^{-(1+2 nu)/(1+z nu)}."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "fixed_conditions": [
    {
      "condition_id": "low_temp_branch",
      "statement": "Temperature T = 10^-6 (dimensionless), corresponding to O(10^-6) nK physical temperature.",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 390,
          "line_end": 390,
          "support": "Panels (a) and (b) show the incompressible kinetic energy E_i at the equilibration time for various quench times tau_Q at temperature T = 10^-6 and T = 1, respectively."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 671,
          "line_end": 671,
          "support": "additional simulations at T=10^-6 (O(10^-6) nK)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
