          "line_start": 390,
          "line_end": 390,
          "support": "Panels (a) and (b) show the incompressible kinetic energy E_i at the equilibration time for various quench times tau_Q at temperature T = 10^-6 and T = 1, respectively."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 671,
          "line_end": 671,
          "support": "at the simulation temperature T=1 (corresponding to a physical temperature of O(1) nK ... and used throughout the main text)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "condition_id": "simulation_parameters",
      "statement": "Simulation parameters: L=30, t_r=10, mu_i=0.1, mu_f=20, g=1, gamma=0.03, epsilon_cut=2.5 mu_f, periodic homogeneous box with V=0.",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 505,
          "line_end": 507,
          "support": "Table with L=30, t_r=10, mu_i=0.1, mu_f=20, g=1, gamma=0.03, T=1, epsilon_cut=2.5 mu_f"
        },
        {
          "line_start": 491,
          "line_end": 491,
          "support": "simulations are performed in a periodic L x L homogeneous box (i.e., V(r)=0)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "condition_id": "equilibration_time_definition",
      "statement": "Equilibration time t_eq is defined as t_2, the end of the interval where the second derivative of N_C/L^2 is <= -Delta, with Delta set to 10% of its maximum.",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 515,
          "line_end": 517,
          "support": "The equilibration time t_eq is identified by analyzing the time evolution of the norm of the order parameter... locate the global maximum of d^2(N_C/L^2)/dt^2 and identify the subsequent interval (t_1,t_2) where d^2(N_C/L^2)/dt^2 <= -Delta, with Delta set to 10% of the maximum. We then take t_eq=t_2."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "controls": [
    {
      "name": "tau_Q",
      "definition": "Quench duration, the time over which the chemical potential is linearly ramped from mu_i to mu_f.",
      "unit": "dimensionless",
      "domain_kind": "continuous_interval",
      "minimum": 100,
      "maximum": 1000,
